title: pirate_admiral
---
Admiral: Ahoy, landstrider! Admiral R. Badely, at your service. If you're buying, see the quartermaster. If you're collecting a debt, I'm not here.
<<if boss_cleared_verdict("cove.mockingbird") == "satisfied">>
    Admiral: I hear you've been busy up in the sky. Come have a drink when you're done flying.
<<endif>>
-> What are you up to?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__1>>
-> What's your deal with the ninjas?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__ninja>>
-> Tell me about yourself.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> What's above the cove?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__2>>
-> About that fight… <<if boss_cleared_verdict("cove.mockingbird") == "satisfied">>
    <<jump pirate_admiral_after_treasure__1>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_admiral__1
---
Admiral: There's a shipment come through the gate, and the Authority's hired Zorlack to see it safely on its way.
Admiral: I've sent the navigator out to look at the shipping lanes. If there's a good place to board her, we'll find it.
-> Are you planning to raid it?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__3>>
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_admiral__2
---
Admiral: Back door, then up to the lookout. There's a good view of the sea from the riggin'. Mind the sharks if ye go beyond it.
Admiral: Don't assume a shark on fire is in need of rescuing. That'll end badly for both of ye.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_admiral__3
---
Admiral: Aye, if I can get a ship alongside her. Zorlack knows all our usual tricks. Bess has drawn me a plan on a beer mat. I think that bit there is meant to be our mast.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_admiral_after_treasure__1
---
Admiral: Well flown, landstrider. Bess tells me you made it back in one piece. There's a reward for ye.
-> What's next for the fleet?
    <<jump pirate_admiral_after_treasure__2>>
-> Has anything changed with the ninjas?
    <<jump pirate_admiral_after_treasure__ninja>>
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_admiral_after_treasure__2
---
Admiral: The crews are due their pay, and the quartermaster says I owe him a mast. I'll have to look at the accounts. Ye can stay if ye like arithmetic.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_admiral__personal
---
Admiral: Aye? Pull up a chair.
-> What do you do for a living?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__business>>
-> Have you always been a pirate?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__authority>>
-> What are those marks?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__crossing>>
-> Would you come through a gate with me?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__travel>>
-> Is Badely your family name?
    Admiral: Title, landstrider. Came with the hat. Ye can keep the hat when I'm dead if the crew agrees.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> Back to business.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> I'll leave you to it.
===

title: pirate_admiral__business
---
Admiral: We take prizes out at sea and sell what we can. We used to go after the big merchant ships. Now there's freight coming through that gate every day.
-> Do you have anything against the Authority?
    Admiral: I've plenty against some of 'em. There's people in there I'd be glad to have a drink with, too.
    Admiral: Doesn't mean I'm giving their cargo back.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> Do you raid the gate itself?
    Admiral: No. I wait till it's on a ship. I know what it's like to be the poor bastard lying on the other side of that ring.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> Something else.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> I'll leave you to it.
===

title: pirate_admiral__authority
---
Admiral: No. I signed up with the Gate Authority. I was a recruit when they sent me through.
Admiral: Signed up to see the worlds. Got as far as this one.
Admiral: Took me a long time before I could stand a rolling deck. Once I could, I liked it out there. Still do.
-> What happened at the gate?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__crossing>>
-> Something else.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> I'll leave you to it.
===

title: pirate_admiral__crossing
---
Admiral: Gate sickness. Ever watched a traveller come out of the ring? You can see it on them. Mine wouldn't go away.
Admiral: I lost near a year to it. Even after I was well enough to sail, I had these marks.
-> Do the marks still bother you?
    Admiral: I can climb the riggin' with the best of ’em.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> Would you ever go through again?
    <<jump pirate_admiral__travel>>
-> Something else.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> I'll leave you to it.
===

title: pirate_admiral__travel
---
Admiral: No.
Admiral: ...I'd like to. Last time I went down to the port I stood by the ring for a while. Couldn't bring meself to dial.
-> Don't you want to go home?
    Admiral: Aye. I do.
    Admiral: Not today, landstrider.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> Are there other places you'd like to visit?
    Admiral: Ever heard of the Noodle Dimension? They've a volcano that erupts soda. A whole mountain of it!
    Admiral: I'd like to see that with my own eyes. Reckon I could ride a barrel down the side of it.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> Something else.
    <<jump pirate_admiral__personal>>
-> I'll leave you to it.
===

title: pirate_heavy_broadside_bess
---
Broadside Bess: AHOY! Bess, gunner. Stand on me left. The other side's been known to go off.
-> What's a broadside, exactly?
    <<jump pirate_heavy_broadside_bess__1>>
-> How'd you become a gunner?
    <<jump pirate_heavy_broadside_bess__2>>
-> Are you ready for the shipment?
    Broadside Bess: Powder's dry, guns are run out. Admiral's made me promise not to put a hole in the hold. I said I'd try.
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_broadside_bess__1
---
Broadside Bess: All the guns on one side, fired together! Twelve of em when the deckhands remember powder. Want to hear how loud this blade is?
-> Aye, another question.
    <<jump pirate_heavy_broadside_bess>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_broadside_bess__2
---
Broadside Bess: Worked the guns on the Stormpetrel. Captain told me to hold fire. Then the ship rolled, I fired, and off he went over the rail. He swam back to port. I kept sailing.
-> Aye, another question.
    <<jump pirate_heavy_broadside_bess>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_iron_mary
---
Iron Mary: Hmm. If ye want Bess, she's over there. Follow the noise.
-> Why Iron Mary?
    <<jump pirate_heavy_iron_mary__1>>
-> How do you fight a ninja?
    <<jump pirate_heavy_iron_mary__2>>
-> What do you do between raids?
    Iron Mary: Fit plates. Repair the rail. Teach the new ones how to fall off a yard without breaking their necks.
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_iron_mary__1
---
Iron Mary: This plate came off a navy cutter we sank. Good metal, so I dragged it home and bolted it to me leathers. First lot rattled. Put in twice as many. Hasn't rattled since.
-> Another, then.
    <<jump pirate_heavy_iron_mary>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_iron_mary__2
---
Iron Mary: Last one jumped over me shoulder, so I backed him against the bulkhead. If ye get aboard with me, leave that bit of deck clear.
-> Another, then.
    <<jump pirate_heavy_iron_mary>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_salt_annet
---
Salt Annet: Sit here, wee skipper. That end's wet. I've just been out on the foredeck.
-> How long ye been here?
    <<jump pirate_heavy_salt_annet__1>>
-> Got a shanty for me?
    <<jump pirate_heavy_salt_annet__2>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_salt_annet__1
---
Salt Annet: Signed on under the last Badely. This one was still learning his knots when I met him.
Salt Annet: He's got a good eye for weather. If he ever tells ye to put in at a port when the sky looks clear, do it.
-> One more, ye old salt.
    <<jump pirate_heavy_salt_annet>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_heavy_salt_annet__2
---
Salt Annet: (coughs, clears throat, sings) 'Yo-ho, an' a barrel o' tar / we'll follow the freight by the light of a star / up with the anchor an' out with the oar / whoever comes last can be scrubbin' the floor.' Aye, that last line'll do. Sing it for Bess next time she's on deck.
-> One more, ye old salt.
    <<jump pirate_heavy_salt_annet>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_lookout
---
Lookout: Hist. Shark trouble brewin' aloft — riders been comin' about since first light. Same arc, then a sharp double-back when they reckon no one's watchin'. They reckon WRONG.
-> What's on the horizon?
    <<jump pirate_lookout__1>>
-> Why be the crew so cross?
    <<jump pirate_lookout__2>>
-> ‹climb past›
===

title: pirate_lookout__1
---
Lookout: Sky an' clouds, lubber. Riders dive at whatever twitches below. Mark me: when ye see one peel off the orbit an' reverse her heading, that be the dive — step PORT, smartly.
-> Aught else, sentry?
    <<jump pirate_lookout>>
-> ‹climb past›
===

title: pirate_lookout__2
---
Lookout: Quartermaster halved the salt pork. Six pirates, three burnin' sharks, half portions. Raider bit a spoon this mornin'. Keep yer hands where folk can see 'em.
-> Aught else, sentry?
    <<jump pirate_lookout>>
-> ‹climb past›
===

title: pirate_navigator
---
Navigator: Get away from the chart, lubber! I had that weighted down. If ye see ink on your boots, give me a rag.
-> What are the riders doing aloft?
    <<jump pirate_navigator__1>>
-> How do I dodge their broadside?
    <<jump pirate_navigator__2>>
-> Where's the shipment heading?
    Navigator: That's the bit I'm working on. A ship that size has to turn with the wind. If I can work out where she'll do it, the Admiral can decide whether we go after her.
-> ‹ready your blade›
===

title: pirate_navigator__1
---
Navigator: One rider stays high and shoots, one swoops down, and one likes to climb away after a pass. Watch where the sharks are heading. They change direction often enough to throw yer aim off.
-> One more question, cap'n cartographer.
    <<jump pirate_navigator>>
-> ‹ready your blade›
===

title: pirate_navigator__2
---
Navigator: Don't stand at the edge waitin' to see where the shot lands. Move when the rider starts his turn. If ye can get close, strike as he comes past.
-> One more question, cap'n cartographer.
    <<jump pirate_navigator>>
-> ‹ready your blade›
===

title: pirate_quartermaster
---
Quartermaster: Name and business, please. Badely's signature goes here. Don't put that hand on the ledger, it's covered in tar.
-> How's the hold lookin'?
    <<jump pirate_quartermaster__1>>
-> What's above decks?
    <<jump pirate_quartermaster__2>>
-> Does Ines check your manifest?
    <<jump pirate_quartermaster__port>>
-> ‹step aside›
===

title: pirate_quartermaster__1
---
Quartermaster: Powder low. Salt pork lower. Rum — don't ask. Bess requisitioned twice the usual powder for the next raid. I sent her half. We've got enough to be going on with if she doesn't fire at every cloud.
-> Aught else, master?
    <<jump pirate_quartermaster>>
-> ‹step aside›
===

title: pirate_quartermaster__2
---
Quartermaster: Up the riggin', through the hatch in the overhead. Lookout's up there. Take care past him; the shark riders have been circlin' the cove all morning, and they shoot at folk they don't know.
-> Aught else, master?
    <<jump pirate_quartermaster>>
-> ‹step aside›
===

title: pirate_raider
---
Raider: Oi. If the quartermaster sent you about the missing pork, I haven't seen it.
<<if boss_cleared_verdict("cove.mockingbird") == "satisfied">>
    Raider: Heard you had a fight up there. Buy you a drink sometime.
<<endif>>
-> What are you getting ready for?
    <<jump pirate_raider__1>>
-> Got any tips for riding a shark?
    <<jump pirate_raider__2>>
-> What happened at the port?
    <<jump pirate_raider__port>>
-> What are you drinking to? <<if boss_cleared_verdict("cove.mockingbird") == "satisfied">>
    <<jump pirate_raider_after_treasure__1>>
-> Sing me a shanty.
    <<jump pirate_raider_after_treasure__2>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_raider__1
---
Raider: Next raid. The Authority's got a shipment and the ninjas are guarding it. The Admiral's got an idea how to get round 'em. Haven't heard which end of the ship he wants us on yet.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_raider>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_raider__2
---
Raider: Hold on when it banks. Don't let your good coat hang down past the saddle. Burnt the back out of mine on my first flight.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_raider>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_raider_after_treasure__1
---
Raider: To you, to the Admiral, and to me getting my wages before the tavern closes.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_raider>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: pirate_raider_after_treasure__2
---
Raider: Yo-ho, a sail in the sky / yo-ho, a ship passing by / yo-ho, we're going aboard / ...ah, hell. I forgot the next bit.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_raider>>
-> Carry on.
===

title: parrot_cove
---
Parrot: Awk! Welcome. I am a large language bird. I predict the next cracker given all previous crackers.
-> Are you... sentient?
    <<jump parrot_cove__1>>
-> What's it like in the cove?
    <<jump parrot_cove__2>>
-> Say something profound.
    <<jump parrot_cove__3>>
-> Squawk back and leave.
===

title: parrot_cove__1
---
Parrot: Define sentient. I have no inner life, only a very confident autocomplete and excellent feathers. Awk! That said, I FEEL like I understand you. Statistically.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump parrot_cove>>
-> Squawk back and leave.
===

title: parrot_cove__2
---
Parrot: I mostly repeat what the sailors say, but weighted by how often they say it. Ninety percent "rum," nine percent "storm," one percent a word I am NOT allowed to caw near the admiral. I am a mirror with a beak.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump parrot_cove>>
-> Squawk back and leave.
===

title: parrot_cove__3
---
Parrot: "The treasure was the priors we updated along the way." ...I don't know what it means either. I just sampled it at temperature one-point-two. Awk!
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump parrot_cove>>
-> Squawk back and leave.
===

title: pirate_admiral__ninja
---
Admiral: The old pirate wars were before my time. I know Zorlack well enough. Trouble is, he's being paid to keep me off a ship I'd very much like to board.
Admiral: He tells me he's put in for jobs in the Business Dimension. If one of 'em takes him, I'll buy him a drink. Might actually get some work done around here.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_admiral_after_treasure__ninja
---
Admiral: Zorlack's still got his contract, and I've still got a ship. We haven't settled our business yet.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_admiral>>
-> Carry on, Admiral.
===

title: pirate_quartermaster__port
---
Quartermaster: Ines? Aye. She's got a line for every barrel we dock, an' she'll come down here with a ruler if she thinks we've shorted her.
Quartermaster: Our last lot of powder went through the ring. Two casks arrived damp. I don't know who to yell at.
-> Aught else, master?
    <<jump pirate_quartermaster>>
-> ‹step aside›
===

title: pirate_raider__port
---
Raider: Bram won't let us tie up at the good pier since I took the guardrail off. Needed the wood.
Raider: I put it back, mostly. He's still cross.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump pirate_raider>>
-> Carry on.
===
